error_signature: "unable to create file .*Invalid argument|Could not reset index file to revision|can't open input file.*build_and_test|幽灵修改|worktree.*No such file or directory"
root_cause: "Two chained Windows worktree pitfalls. (1) origin/main contains a committed filename ending in two CR characters (archives/g/gama/2.29/patches/0002-dataparser-ungated.patch\\r\\r); Win32 cannot create files with control characters, so ANY full checkout of origin/main on Windows fails at 100% with 'Invalid argument' and git rolls back the worktree. (2) 'git worktree add' seeds the new worktree's index from the current repo's index, which carries skip-worktree bits (for files Windows cannot materialize) and staged user content — a subsequent read-tree/checkout can materialize files whose bytes come from the MAIN worktree's staged blobs, producing phantom modifications in a brand-new worktree."
rec_approach: "Create the worktree with --no-checkout; write sparse-checkout patterns directly into <main>/.git/worktrees/<lib>/info/sparse-checkout with printf (bypassing Git Bash MSYS path mangling which silently rewrites '!/archives/' into '!C:/Program Files/Git/archives/'); exclude archives/ and re-include your own package dir; then run 'git read-tree -u --reset HEAD' (--reset discards the inherited index — note '-mu --reset' is an invalid flag combination); finally require 'git status --short' to be completely empty before starting any work. Long-term fix is renaming the CR-suffixed file from a Linux checkout."
match_keywords: ["worktree add", "Invalid argument", "Could not reset index file", "carriage return filename", "sparse-checkout", "read-tree", "--reset", "skip-worktree", "index copy", "MSYS path conversion", "phantom modification", "幽灵修改", "检出失败", "Windows"]
error_excerpt: "error: unable to create file archives/g/gama/2.29/patches/0002-dataparser-ungated.patch??: Invalid argument\nfatal: Could not reset index file to revision 'HEAD'."
severity: P1
category: git\|workflow\|windows\|worktree
last_updated: 2026-09-27
